      "writtenOn": "2024-03-30T01:41:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a quite common operation that should probably be in a library. It doesn\u0027t seem like every user of Fontations should need to know this level of minutia for the common task of just wanting a family or style name. For instance, FreeType exposes this as `family_name` and `style_name` with DirectWrite providing a more modern (and more like Fontations) IDWriteFontFamily::GetFamilyNames (family names, like this) and IDWriteFont::GetFaceNames (style names, like \"Regular\" or \"Bold\") which return a set of localized strings much like `localized_strings` but automatically pick the `StringId`.\n\nPerhaps that what Fontations should expose, a `FontRef.family_name() -\u003e StringId` and a `FontRef.style_name() -\u003e StringId` which would look at the WWS and which name ids are available and return which `StringId` should be requested. (They could also return the appropriate `LocalizedStrings` directly if that makes sense.)",
      "revId": "85a889abfdf9d77ebf8a59e20d74df0c39b38545",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
